{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBRVLG7V3XF9mJBNZNqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 9** (In 0.716 / Sb 0.284). It had the highest EQE of the three compositions I measured, but the margin over index 14 is small and much of the library was never measured.\n\n| Index | In / Sb | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0.851 / 0.149 | 0.018 |\n| **9** | **0.716 / 0.284** | **0.039** |\n| 14 | 0.528 / 0.472 | 0.036 |\n\nAll three values are very low, so the whole In–Sb oxide line looks like a weak photoanode under 2.7 eV light.\n\n**What the XRD showed:** I used 4 of the 5 XRD scans, on indices 4, 10, 15 and 22.\n- **Indium-rich side (up to about 34% Sb):** the patterns match cubic In₂O₃ (bixbyite), with its peaks getting weaker as Sb increases.\n- **Rutile InSbO₄:** its peak first appears at about 50% Sb and is still there at 73% Sb.\n- **Peaks in every pattern** (Q ≈ 2.79, 4.55, 5.33 Å⁻¹) look like they come from the substrate.\n\nEQE doubled from index 2 to index 9 and dipped only slightly at index 14. So the best composition probably lies between about 28% and 47% Sb, near where the InSbO₄ phase starts to form.\n\n**A mistake that cost the result:** I spent all three EQE measurements at once instead of one at a time. Measuring in sequence would have let me put the third measurement between indices 9 and 14, after seeing that both were similar and well above index 2. Indices 10–13 sit in that gap and were never measured, so one of them could beat index 9. The Sb-rich end (indices 15–27) is also unmeasured. I didn't expect much there, because InSbO₄'s wide band gap should absorb poorly at 2.7 eV, but that is a guess, not a measurement."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":8682,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":607},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7492e82-5d53-4399-9a01-3d0b7943df60","uuid":"fb1ee2d2-7e71-4c49-96b0-96d5fdfca406","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:02:38.437Z","request_id":"req_011CfBRVKk7D5eMYU15FGPGH"}
